.TH ASUS-CONTROL-CENTER 1 "October 2026" "asus-control-center 0.4.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
asus-control-center \- battery, performance, GPU and display controls for ASUS laptops
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B asus-control-center
.RB [ \-\-specs | \-\-self\-test ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B asus-control-center
is a GTK 4 / libadwaita app that shows the hardware of an ASUS laptop and
the controls its firmware exposes: battery charge limit and charging mode,
performance profile, GPU MUX and iGPU-only mode, keyboard backlight, fan and
temperature readings, and display dimming.
.PP
Controls that change hardware run
.I /usr/libexec/asus-control-center/acc-helper
through
.BR pkexec (1),
which asks for an administrator password. The helper accepts only a fixed
list of actions and values.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-specs
Print the hardware report and which controls this machine supports, then
exit. Nothing is written.
.TP
.B \-\-self\-test
Same report as
.BR \-\-specs ,
then check the sign-in crypto. Exits non-zero if that check fails.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ACC_DEBUG
When set, print debugging output to standard error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/asus-control-center/
Stylesheets, images and the bundled Soft Brightness Plus GNOME Shell
extension.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/gnome-shell/extensions/soft-brightness-plus@joelkitching.com/
Where the extension is copied when OLED dimming is turned on.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR asusctl (1),
.BR supergfxctl (1),
.BR pkexec (1)
.SH BUGS
https://github.com/Mostafamomen/asus-control-center/issues
